; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17
; Page: 132
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The Gmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777223


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-str-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: ST-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17
; Page: 132
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The Gmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777223


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17
; Page: 132
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The Gmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777223


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-asr-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Abort-Session-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17
; Page: 132
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The Gmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777223


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aar-trace-activation)
; AVP: Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info
; Command: AA-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.1
; Page: 143
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When used for these purposes, the Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info AVP shall not be included."
"The AAR command is also used when the GGSN needs to activate a Trace Session in the BM-SC. In this case the Called-Station-Id AVP, Calling-Station-Id AVP, Framed-IP-Address AVP, Framed-IPv6-Prefix AVP, Framed-Interface-Id AVP, and RAI AVP shall not be included."
    excludes Called-Station-Id or Calling-Station-Id or Framed-IP-Address or Framed-IPv6-Prefix or Framed-Interface-Id or RAI


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aar-modification)
; AVP: Called-Station-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.1
; Page: 143
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the AAR command is used by the GGSN to modify an MBMS UE context in the BM-SC, it shall include all the parameters that have been changed according to the triggering Update MBMS Context Request, ref. fig. 35."
"The Called-Station-Id AVP, Calling-Station-Id AVP, Framed-IP-Address AVP, Framed-IPv6-Prefix AVP and Framed-Interface-Id AVP shall not be included,"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aaa-trace-alternative-apn)
; AVP: Alternative-APN
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.2
; Page: 144
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the AAA command is used to acknowledge an AAR that activated a Trace Session, the only Gmb specific AVP that shall be included is the 3GPP-IMSI AVP."
    absent-if request/Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aaa-trace-imsi)
; AVP: 3GPP-IMSI
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.2
; Page: 144
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the AAA command is used to acknowledge an AAR that activated a Trace Session, the only Gmb specific AVP that shall be included is the 3GPP-IMSI AVP."
    present-if request/Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aaa-trace-tmgi)
; AVP: TMGI
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.2
; Page: 144
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the AAA command is used to acknowledge an AAR that activated a Trace Session, the only Gmb specific AVP that shall be included is the 3GPP-IMSI AVP."
    absent-if request/Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-aaa-trace-bearer-capabilities)
; AVP: Required-MBMS-Bearer-Capabilities
; Command: AA-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.2
; Page: 144
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the AAA command is used to acknowledge an AAR that activated a Trace Session, the only Gmb specific AVP that shall be included is the 3GPP-IMSI AVP."
    absent-if request/Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-str-trace-deactivation)
; AVP: Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info
; Command: ST-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.3
; Page: 144
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The Gmb specific AVP Additonal-MBMS-Trace-Info shall be included in the STR command only in the case of a Trace Session deactivation."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-update-service-area)
; AVP: MBMS-Service-Area
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.5
; Page: 145
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Session Update procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC in order for the GGSN(s) to update their session attributes. The updated MBMS-Service-Area AVP shall be included. The MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP with the value UPDATE shall be included."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = UPDATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-update-time-to-data-transfer)
; AVP: MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.5
; Page: 145
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP with the value UPDATE shall be included. The MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer with the value set to 0 shall be included."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = UPDATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-update-session-duration)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Duration
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.5
; Page: 145
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Session-Duration AVP shall be included to indicate the duration of the remaining part of the MBMS session."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = UPDATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-update-sgsn-address)
; AVP: 3GPP-SGSN-Address
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.6.5
; Page: 145
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The 3GPP-SGSN-Address AVP and the 3GPP-SGSN-IPv6-Address AVP shall be included if the related lists of downstream nodes in the GGSN(s) have changed."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#tmgi-element)
; AVP: TMGI
; Section: 17.7.2
; Page: 150
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The encoding of TMGI is specified in 3GPP TS 24.008 [54]."
    encoding element TS24.008 10.5.6.13 "Temporary Mobile Group Identity"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#required-bearer-capabilities-element)
; AVP: Required-MBMS-Bearer-Capabilities
; Section: 17.7.3
; Page: 150
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The information contained in this AVP is UTF-8 encoded MBMS bearer capabilities as defined in 3GPP TS 24.008 [54]."
    encoding element TS24.008 10.5.6.14 "MBMS bearer capabilities"


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-StartStop-Indication
; Section: 17.7.5
; Page: 150
MBMS-StartStop-Indication ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 902 10415 >
        START     = 0
        STOP      = 1
        UPDATE    = 2
        HEARTBEAT = 3


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-service-area-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-Service-Area
; Section: 17.7.6
; Page: 151
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The length of an MBMS service area code is 2 octets."
"Number N of MBMS service area codes coded as: 1 binary value is ‘00000000’ 256 binary value is '11111111'"
"A consecutive list of N MBMS service area codes"
    length 3..513 octets
"Each MBMS service area code shall only be present once in the list."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-session-duration-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Duration
; Section: 17.7.7
; Page: 151
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Session-Duration AVP (AVP code 904) is of type OctetString with a length of three octets and indicates the estimated session duration (MBMS Service data transmission)."
    length 3 octets
"Bit 8 of octet 1 to bit 8 of octet 3 (17 bits) express seconds, for which the maximum allowed value is 86400 seconds. Bits 7 to 1 of octet 3 (7 bits) express days, for which the maximum allowed value is 18 days."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-Service-Type
; Section: 17.7.9
; Page: 151
MBMS-Service-Type ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 906 10415 >
        MULTICAST = 0
        BROADCAST = 1


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-2G-3G-Indicator
; Section: 17.7.10
; Page: 152
MBMS-2G-3G-Indicator ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 907 10415 >
        2G        = 0
        3G        = 1
        2G-AND-3G = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-session-identity-octet)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Identity
; Section: 17.7.11
; Page: 152
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Session-Identity AVP (AVP code 908) is of type OctetString. Its length is one octet."
    length 1 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#rai-octets)
; AVP: RAI
; Section: 17.7.12
; Page: 152
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"Its value shall be encoded as a UTF-8 string on either 11 (if the MNC contains two digits) or 12 (if the MNC contains three digits) octets as follows:"
    length 11..12 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#additional-mbms-trace-info-element)
; AVP: Additional-MBMS-Trace-Info
; Section: 17.7.13
; Page: 152
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"This AVP contains Trace Reference2, Trace Recording Session Reference, Triggering Events in BM-SC, Trace Depth for BM-SC, List of interfaces in BM-SC, Trace Activity Control For BM-SC which are all part of the Additional MBMS Trace Info IE as specified in TS 29.060 [24]."
    encoding element TS29.060 7.7.68 "Additional MBMS Trace Info"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#time-to-data-transfer-octet)
; AVP: MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer
; Section: 17.7.14
; Page: 152
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer AVP (AVP code 911) is of type OctetString. Its length is one octet."
    length 1 octets
"The coding is specified as per the Time to MBMS Data Transfer Value Part Coding of the Time to MBMS Data Transfer IE in 3GPP TS 48.018 [70]."
    encoding element TS48.018 11.3.92 "Time to MBMS Data Transfer"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#session-repetition-number-octet)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number
; Section: 17.7.15
; Page: 153
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number AVP (AVP code 912) is of type OctetString with a length of one octet."
    length 1 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-start-repetition-number)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.7.15
; Page: 153
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the optional MBMS-Session-Identity AVP is included in the MBMS Session Start RAR (Start) command by the BM-SC, the BM-SC shall also provide the corresponding MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number AVP, and vice versa."
    present-if MBMS-Session-Identity and MBMS-StartStop-Indication = START


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gmb-rar-start-session-identity)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Identity
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777223
; Section: 17.7.15
; Page: 153
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"When the optional MBMS-Session-Identity AVP is included in the MBMS Session Start RAR (Start) command by the BM-SC, the BM-SC shall also provide the corresponding MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number AVP, and vice versa."
    present-if MBMS-Session-Repetition-Number and MBMS-StartStop-Indication = START


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-required-qos-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-Required-QoS
; Section: 17.7.16
; Page: 153
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"QoS Profile as specified by the Quality-of-Service information element, from octet 3 onwards, in 3GPP TS 24.008 [54]."
    text-only


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-Counting-Information
; Section: 17.7.17
; Page: 153
MBMS-Counting-Information ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 914 10415 >
        COUNTING-NOT-APPLICABLE = 0
        COUNTING-APPLICABLE     = 1


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-User-Data-Mode-Indication
; Section: 17.7.18
; Page: 153
MBMS-User-Data-Mode-Indication ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 915 10415 >
        Unicast                 = 0
        "Multicast and Unicast" = 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#user-data-mode-default)
; AVP: MBMS-User-Data-Mode-Indication
; Section: 17.7.18
; Page: 153
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The absence of this AVP indicates unicast mode of operation."
    default Unicast


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-ggsn-address-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-GGSN-Address
; Section: 17.7.19
; Page: 154
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-GGSN-Address AVP (AVP code 916) is of type OctetString, and contains the value of GGSN’s Ipv4 address for user plane data."
    length 4 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-ggsn-ipv6-address-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-GGSN-IPv6-Address
; Section: 17.7.20
; Page: 154
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-GGSN-Ipv6-Address AVP (AVP code 917) is of type OctetString, and contains the value of GGSN’s Ipv6 address for user plane data."
    length 16 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#bmsc-ssm-ip-address-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-BMSC-SSM-IP-Address
; Section: 17.7.21
; Page: 154
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-BMSC-SSM-IP-Address AVP (AVP code 918) is of type OctetString, and contains the value of BM-SC’s IPv4 address for Source Specific Multicasting."
    length 4 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#bmsc-ssm-ipv6-address-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-BMSC-SSM-IPv6-Address
; Section: 17.7.22
; Page: 154
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-BMSC-SSM-IPv6-Address AVP (AVP code 919) is of type OctetString, and contains the value of BM-SC’s IPv6 address for Source Specific Multicasting."
    length 16 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#mbms-flow-identifier-octets)
; AVP: MBMS-Flow-Identifier
; Section: 17.7.23
; Page: 154
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The MBMS-Flow-Identifier AVP (AVP code 920) is of type OctetString. Its length is two octets."
    length 2 octets


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: CN-IP-Multicast-Distribution
; Section: 17.7.24
; Page: 154
CN-IP-Multicast-Distribution ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 921 10415 >
        NO-IP-MULTICAST = 0
        IP-MULTICAST    = 1


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-HC-Indicator
; Section: 17.7.25
; Page: 154
; Values: 3GPP TS 25.413 [92]
MBMS-HC-Indicator ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 922 10415 >
        uncompressed-header = 0 ;; supplied: (TS29.061.py#mbms-hc-indicator-values)
        compressed-header   = 1 ;; supplied: (TS29.061.py#mbms-hc-indicator-values)


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Experimental-Result-Code
; Kind: result-codes
; Section: 17.8
; Page: 155
DIAMETER_ERROR_START_INDICATION            = 5120 ; 17.8.2
DIAMETER_ERROR_STOP_INDICATION             = 5121 ; 17.8.2
DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_MBMS_BEARER_SERVICE = 5122 ; 17.8.2
DIAMETER_ERROR_SERVICE_AREA                = 5123 ; 17.8.2
DIAMETER_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES            = 4121 ; 17.8.3


; Type: Value Table
; AVP: Experimental-Result-Code
; Kind: result-codes
; Section: 19.5
; Page: 163
DIAMETER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_MBMS_BEARER_SERVICE = 5122 ; 19.5.2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.1
; Page: 163
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The SGmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777292


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-str-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: ST-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.1
; Page: 163
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The SGmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777292


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-asr-auth-application-id)
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Abort-Session-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.1
; Page: 163
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The SGmb application identifier value shall be included in the Auth-Application-Id AVP."
    range 16777292


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-str-path-failure)
; AVP: Diagnostic-Info
; Command: ST-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.3.3
; Page: 166
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"If the MBMS GW detects the SGi-mb path failure as specified in subclause 20.3.2.1 of 3GPP TS 23.007 [104], the MBMS GW shall set the Termination-Cause to \"DIAMETER_LINK_BROKEN\" (see IETF RFC 6733 [111]) and shall include the Diagnostic-Info AVP set to \"User Plane Failure\" if it tears down the MBMS session as a result of detecting an SGi-mb path failure."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-time-to-data-transfer)
; AVP: MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Session Start procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC to the MBMS GW(s) that will deliver the MBMS service when it is ready to send data."
"The MBMS-Time-to-Data-Transfer AVP shall be included to indicate the expected time between the reception of the MBMS Session Start and the transmission of MBMS data flows."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = START
"For the MBMS Session Update procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC in order for the MBMS GW(s) to update their session attributes."
"The MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP with the value UPDATE shall be included. The MBMS-Time-To-Data-Transfer with AVP the value set to 0 shall be included."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = UPDATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-service-area)
; AVP: MBMS-Service-Area
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Session Start procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC to the MBMS GW(s) that will deliver the MBMS service when it is ready to send data."
"The RAR message shall also contain the MBMS-Service-Area AVP."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = START
"If the MBMS service area or the MBMS cell list needs to be changed, the MBMS-Service-Area AVP shall be included in the RAR."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-local-m1-information)
; AVP: Local-M1-Information
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"The RAR message shall also contain the Local-M1-Information AVP if the BM-SC determines to use the local MBMS information as specified in 3GPP TS 23.285 [112]."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-cell-list)
; AVP: MBMS-Cell-List
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"If the MBMS Cell List feature is supported and the MBMS cell list needs to be changed, the MBMS-Cell-List AVP shall also be included."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-update-session-duration)
; AVP: MBMS-Session-Duration
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Session Update procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC in order for the MBMS GW(s) to update their session attributes."
"The MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP with the value UPDATE shall be included."
"The MBMS-Session-Duration AVP shall be included to indicate the duration of the remaining part of the MBMS session."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = UPDATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-heartbeat-restart-counter)
; AVP: Restart-Counter
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.1
; Page: 168
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Heartbeat procedure, RAR is sent by the BM-SC to the MBMS GW, or vice-versa. The RAR message shall contain the following AVPs:"
"the MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP set to the value \"heartbeat\";"
"the Restart-Counter AVP set to the local restart counter of the sender."
    present-if MBMS-StartStop-Indication = HEARTBEAT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-raa-heartbeat-indication)
; AVP: MBMS-StartStop-Indication
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.2
; Page: 170
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Heartbeat procedure, RAA is sent by the BM-SC to the MBMS GW, or vice-versa. The RAA message shall contain the following AVPs:"
"the MBMS-StartStop-Indication AVP set to the value \"heartbeat\";"
    present-if request/MBMS-StartStop-Indication = HEARTBEAT and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS
    values 3 if request/MBMS-StartStop-Indication = HEARTBEAT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-raa-heartbeat-restart-counter)
; AVP: Restart-Counter
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.4.2
; Page: 170
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"For the MBMS Heartbeat procedure, RAA is sent by the BM-SC to the MBMS GW, or vice-versa. The RAA message shall contain the following AVPs:"
"the Restart-Counter AVP set to the local restart counter of the sender."
    present-if request/MBMS-StartStop-Indication = HEARTBEAT and Result-Code = DIAMETER_SUCCESS


; Type: Enumerated AVP
; Name: MBMS-Access-Indicator
; Section: 20.5a.1
; Page: 175
MBMS-Access-Indicator ::= < Enumerated AVP header: 923 10415 >
        UTRAN             = 0
        E-UTRAN           = 1
        UTRAN-AND-E-UTRAN = 2


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#gw-ssm-ip-address-octets)
