; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-rar-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.7
; Page: 178
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"On the SGmb reference point, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints ;; interpreted: (TS29.061.dadx#sgmb-raa-supported-features-vendor)
; AVP: Supported-Features
; Command: Re-Auth-Answer
; Application-ID: 16777292
; Section: 20.7
; Page: 178
; Versions: 18.1.0..19.1.0
"On the SGmb reference point, the Supported-Features AVP is used to identify features that have been defined by 3GPP and hence, for features defined in this document, the Vendor-Id AVP shall contain the vendor ID of 3GPP (10415)."
    text-only
"If the RAR command contains the Supported-Features AVP, the MBMS GW shall include the Supported-Features AVP in the RAA command, with the ‘M’ bit cleared, indicating only the features that both the BM-SC and MBMS GW support."
    text-only
